    ("ax:unknown", "Until a design is implemented and used, nobody can be sure how well it works, and even then those voting on it cannot fully judge how well it serves users. A design with more parts and more interactions with existing wording has more places where a defect can go unnoticed.", "'a room polling on it' is 'those voting on it'"),
    ("ax:first-review", "When a proposal is first presented, it has received less committee review than at any later meeting. When a design is presented in parts, reviewers of an early part cannot study in detail what the later parts will require of it until those parts are presented.", "split in two"),
