    ("ax:turnover", "Over the years, some participants stop attending and others join, while a published paper stays available to later readers for decades. Someone absent from a meeting learns what was said there only from writing or from those present who remember it, and a clear written objection is easier to raise again.", "same four clauses, regrouped"),
    ("ax:users-affected", "A design in the standard applies to every user of its feature, so a better design's gain is spread across them all, while participating costs the participant or their sponsor. Users differ from each other and from participants in the features they care about and what they can spend taking part, and one user's effort seldom changes a committee outcome.", "'the chance ... is small' is 'seldom'"),
    ("d:rooms", "A design room is EWG or LEWG, a study group is any WG21 study group, a wording room is CWG or LWG, and a subgroup is any of these. Plenary is a WG21 meeting's closing plenary session, a chair chairs a subgroup, the convenor convenes WG21, and a consensus call is a chair's or the convenor's determination of consensus.", ""),
    ("d:national-body", "A national body is an ISO member body that is a P-member of SC22, the committee WG21 belongs to. In quotations from the Directives, \"the committee\" is SC22, \"the Chair\" its chair, and \"National Body\" any ISO member body, which on enquiry and final ballots includes non-P-members of SC22.", ""),
